{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And it came to pass at the end.</b> Scripture did not specify the beginning of this reckoning, and likewise \"And it came to pass after forty years\" (II Samuel 15:7), and likewise \"and within sixty-five years\" (Isaiah 7:8), and likewise \"And it came to pass in the thirtieth year\" (Ezekiel 1:1). It is possible that this reckoning is from the departure of the chief cupbearer from the prison house, or from Joseph's sitting there." "And the meaning of \"days\" I have already explained:" "<b>And Pharaoh dreamed.</b> He was dreaming, and likewise \"and Rebekah was listening\" (Genesis 27:5):"], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:47:36.543718012Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}